      262.89
    ],
    "text": "7.(1) It shall be lawful for the Corporation, from timeto time, at any general meeting and by the votes of not lessthan two thirds of the members present and voting, to makerules, not inconsistent with the provisions of this Act or anyother written law, for all or any of the following matters:\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Bold",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      172.87,
      273.55,
      397.28,
      310.89
    ],
    "text": "(a)classification of membership, fees payable by eachclass of members and admission, withdrawal,expulsion or resignation of members;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      172.87,
      321.55,
      397.05,
      358.89
    ],
    "text": "(b)election of the Council, resignation or removal from,or vacation of, office as office bearers and powers,duties and conduct of the Council;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      173.71,
      369.55,
      397.31,
      394.89
    ],
    "text": "(c)powers, duties and functions of the various officers,agents and servants of the Corporation;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      172.87,
      405.55,
      397.35,
      466.89
    ],
    "text": "(d)procedure relating to the summoning and holdingof meetings of the Council and the Corporationand any sub-committee thereof, including thequorum therefor and the conduct of businessthereat;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      173.71,
      477.55,
      397.02,
      502.89
    ],
    "text": "(e)qualification and disqualification for membershipin the Corporation and in the Council;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      175.15,
      513.55,
      397.12,
      538.89
    ],
    "text": "(f)administration and management of the property ofthe Corporation; and",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      172.87,
      549.55,
      397.15,
      574.89
    ],
    "text": "(g)generally for the management of the affairs of theCorporation and the attainment of its objects.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      585.55,
      397.12,
      670.89
    ],
    "text": "(2) The Articles of the Association in force on the daypreceding the date of commencement of this Act shall, in sofar as they are not inconsistent with the provisions of the Actor any other written law, be deemed to be the rules of theCorporation and may be amended, altered, added to orrescinded at a like meeting and in like manner as a rule madeunder subsection (1) of this section.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
